### **B. Classification of Organic Compounds**
Organic compounds are categorized based on their carbon skeleton:

| Main Category | Sub-Category | Definition / Characteristics |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Acyclic / Open Chain** | **Saturated** | Only single bonds ($C-C$). No $\pi$-bonds. |
| | **Unsaturated** | Contains at least one double or triple bond ($\pi$-bonds). |
| **Cyclic / Closed Chain** | **Homocyclic (Carbocyclic)** | The ring consists **only** of Carbon atoms. |
| | **Heterocyclic** | The ring contains at least one atom other than Carbon (O, N, S, etc.). |
| | **Alicyclic** | Cyclic compounds that behave like aliphatic (open chain) compounds. |
| | **Aromatic** | Specialized stable rings (e.g., Benzene). Detailed in GOC. |
