## **5. Problem-Solving Framework**

| Question Type | Identification Clues | Approach / Strategy |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Epoxy Naming** | Oxygen bridged between carbons. | Identify locants x, y; name as **x,y-epoxy**. |
| **3+ Identical Groups** | 3 \\(-COOH, -CN\\), etc. | If all direct: use **Carbo-** suffix. If not: use **Prefixes**. |
| **Bicyclo Numbering** | Shared bridgehead atoms. | **Bridgehead \\(\rightarrow\\) Large Bridge \\(\rightarrow\\) Small Bridge**. |
| **Ester with Side Chains** | \\(R-CO-OR'\\) with epoxy/ether. | Name \\(R'\\) (on Oxygen) first, then locants and suffixes. |

