## **8. Common Mistakes and Traps**

| Mistake | Why Students Make It | Correct Approach / Thinking |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Counting \\(C\\) of \\(CN\\) on ring** | Treating it like an open chain. | Use **Carbonitrile**; do not number the Carbon of the functional group. |
| **Mixing Bicyclo Bridge numbers** | Writing them in ascending order. | Numbers in the bracket \\([x.y.z]\\) must be in **descending order**. |
| **Numbering from the "Middle"** | Trying to give side chains #1. | Always start at a **Bridgehead** carbon for Bicyclo. |
| **Ignoring "VIP" in Esters** | Mixing the \\(R'\\) group with other side chains. | The group on **Oxygen** is always named **first and separately**. |

